Package: netinf
Title: Diagnostics for Influential Cases in Network Analysis
Version: 0.1.0.0
Authors@R:
    c(person("Borui", "Yang", , "yangborui859@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0006-7532-8950")),
    person("Shu Fai", "Cheung", , "shufai.cheung@gmail.com", role = c("aut"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9871-9448")))
Description: Provides tools to identify influential cases in network analysis.
    This package complements 'bootnet' (Epskamp, Borsboom, and Fried, 2018) <doi:10.3758/s13428-017-0862-1> by adding a
    complete workflow for influence diagnostics: extracting case indices
    from bootstrap samples, computing empirical influence values via
    regression on inclusion counts, validating candidate cases via
    leave-one-out and leave-multiple-out analysis, and quantifying
    centrality changes via a generalized Cook's distance.
